  "description": "bike-race madness. It's all\nthe fun you can stand. A 'cross race is lap after lap around a dirt course\nyou can't entirely ride; You've got to run some of it with your bike on\nyour shoulder. Crazy-popular in New England, Colorado, the Pacific Northwest\nand the SF Bay Area, 'cross is changing, growing, going mainstream.\n\nCross may be the most-changed \"road\" Fuji for 2002, most upgraded.\nThe frame (six sizes) is now X-Fusion Alpha tubing, lighter when you're\npedaling it, lighter when you're carrying it. The fork is now aluminum\ntoo, a cross-specific model with an 1 1/8\" steerer.\n\nThe components are nearly unchanged except for the crankset, an FSA this\nyear, with 38-48 chainrings and ISIS bottom bracket. And the new for '02\ncustom saddle. The bars, stem, wheels and tires are Ritchey.\n\nSo much for parts. A Fuji Cross is a wonderfully versatile bicycle. It's\nnearly as effective off-road as a mountain bike and way more fun. Put\nsmooth-tread tires on it and it makes a great road bike. Put lights and\nfenders on it and ride it to and from work or to and from Yellowstone.\n\nIf you can only have one bike... Cross. Questions?",
